  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Albanian Railways</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of a sovereign loan of up to EUR 36.87 million to the Republic of  Albania for the benefit of Albanian Railways (&quot;HSH&quot;, the &quot;Client&quot; or the  &quot;Company&quot;) to finance:  i) the rehabilitation and upgrade of approximately 34.7 km railway line  between the Tirana Public Transport Terminal (&quot;PTT&quot;) and the city of Durres; and  ii) the construction of an approximately 7.4 km railway branch line to the  Tirana International Airport (&quot;TIA&quot;) (together &quot;the Project&quot;).   An increase by up to EUR 40.7 million of the existing sovereign loan of EUR  36.87 million in favour of the Republic of Albania was provided to finance:  i) the construction of approximately eight stations and stops along the  Tirana-Durres railway line and along the new rail connection to TIA;  ii) cost increases resulting from price adjustments and design improvements;  and  iii) additional works supervision services.  An additional loan increase by up to EUR 11.62 million will be provided to  co-finance the electrification of the railway lines financed under the Project,  namely, the Tirana PTT - Durres railway line, and the new rail link to TIA.  The Project is co-financed by the European Union (&quot;EU&quot;) through the Western  Balkans Investment Framework (&quot;WBIF&quot;) which has provided investment grants in  the amount of up to EUR 32.94 million and technical assistance grants in the  amount of up to EUR 2.5 million. Additional WBIF grants are expected to be  provided to co-finance the Project&apos;s electrification component.  The Project is part of Route 2 of the Western Balkans Core Network connecting  the cities of Podgorica in Montenegro and Vlore in Albania and has been  established as an indicative extension to theTrans-European Transport Networks  (TEN-T) to the Western Balkans core railway network. The Project will support  Albania&apos;s economic development and contribute to its regional integration by  improving connectivity between the cities of Tirana and Durres and TIA.</narrative>
  </description>
